Make the three operating-mode constants visible without the layered driver.

WHY THIS EXISTS.  R6b-8 8b built CONFIG_RTL_819X_SWCORE=n as a variant; since
8g it is `quiet` and `loud` in config/rlxfw-kernel.delta.  量 2026-09-27, probe cell
r6b8bp0 (that one delta row, no seam): the build does not reach the link.
net/rtl/features/rtl_features.c fails to COMPILE -- `GATEWAY_MODE'
undeclared at :1103, `WISP_MODE' at :1117, `BRIDGE_MODE' at :1125, all in
rtl865x_getWanDev(), which is compiled under
`CONFIG_NET_SCHED && CONFIG_RTL_IPTABLES_FAST_PATH` (:1097); both stay y.
讀 include/net/rtl/rtl_nic.h:213-246: the three #defines sit inside
`#ifdef CONFIG_RTL_LAYERED_DRIVER`, a symbol the SWCORE block declares, so
SWCORE=n takes them from the one file outside the block that still reads
them.  The segment-113 design's census counted references to vendor SYMBOLS
through a host preprocessor and could not see a missing MACRO; it concluded
that no vendor line need change, and this build refutes that.

WHAT IT DOES.  Two lines of the header change and none is added or removed:
the blank line after RTL865X_CONFIG_END becomes the `#endif`, and the
commented-out MULTIPLE_VLAN_BRIDGE_MODE line becomes
`#ifdef CONFIG_RTL_LAYERED_DRIVER`, with that comment kept after it.  The
three constants are then defined whatever CONFIG_RTL_LAYERED_DRIVER says;
struct rtl865x_vlanConfig, RTL865X_CONFIG_END, CONFIG_CHECK and INIT_CHECK
stay under it.

WHY IT IS INERT AT SWCORE=y.  With CONFIG_RTL_LAYERED_DRIVER defined -- the
mainline, and every image built before this patch -- both halves are
included, so the preprocessor emits the tokens the unpatched header gives,
and no line moves, so no __LINE__ does.  PREDICTION, written before the
mainline build: that build's objects are byte-identical to r6b8cr's except
those whose inputs 8b changes -- the seam object, the two consumers of
RLXFW_SRC_ID (init/main.o and drivers/mtd/devices/rtl819x-spi.o), and the
links that carry them.  REFUTED BY any other object differing --
net/rtl/features/rtl_features.o first.

WHAT IT DOES NOT DO.  It defines no storage: rtl865x_getWanDev() reads
rtl865x_curOpMode, which at SWCORE=n is the seam's
(config/rlxfw-src/linux-2.6.30/drivers/net/rlxfw-seam.c, the vendor's
GATEWAY_MODE, 0).  With no vendor netdev it finds neither ppp0 nor eth1 and
returns NULL; its one caller in the fast path (net/rtl/fastpath/96E/
fastpath_core.S:785) is in the NAPT-entry path, which no rlxfw image
configures (推).

